{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CatchBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" component is a component that catches errors thrown by its children, renders an error component and optionally calls the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCatch"},{"type":"text","value":" callback. It also accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getResetKey"},{"type":"text","value":" function that can be used to declaratively reset the component's state when the key changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"catchboundary-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CatchBoundary props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CatchBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the following props:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-getresetkey-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.getResetKey"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that returns a string that will be used to reset the component's state when the key changes."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-children-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.children"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.ReactNode"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component's children to render when there is no error"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-errorcomponent-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.errorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.ReactNode"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional - "},{"type":"link","href":"./errorComponentComponent.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"default: ErrorComponent"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component to render when there is an error."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-oncatch-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.onCatch"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error: unknown, errorInfo: ErrorInfo) => void"},{"type":"text","value":" in React; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error: unknown) => void"},{"type":"text","value":" in Vue; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error: Error) => void"},{"type":"text","value":" in Solid"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A callback that will be called with the error that was thrown by the component's children."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"catchboundary-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CatchBoundary returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the component's children if there is no error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" if there is an error."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { CatchBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <CatchBoundary\n      getResetKey={() => 'reset'}\n      onCatch={(error) => console.error(error)}\n    >\n      <div>My Component</div>\n    </CatchBoundary>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"catchboundary-props","text":"CatchBoundary props","level":2},{"id":"props-getresetkey-prop","text":"props.getResetKey prop","level":3},{"id":"props-children-prop","text":"props.children prop","level":3},{"id":"props-errorcomponent-prop","text":"props.errorComponent prop","level":3},{"id":"props-oncatch-prop","text":"props.onCatch prop","level":3},{"id":"catchboundary-returns","text":"CatchBoundary returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `CatchBoundary` component is a component that catches errors thrown by its children, renders an error component and optionally calls the `onCatch` callback. It also accepts a `getResetKey` function that can be used to declaratively reset the component's state when the key changes.\n\n## CatchBoundary props\n\nThe `CatchBoundary` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.getResetKey` prop\n\n- Type: `() => string`\n- Required\n- A function that returns a string that will be used to reset the component's state when the key changes.\n\n### `props.children` prop\n\n- Type: `React.ReactNode`\n- Required\n- The component's children to render when there is no error\n\n### `props.errorComponent` prop\n\n- Type: `React.ReactNode`\n- Optional - [`default: ErrorComponent`](./errorComponentComponent.md)\n- The component to render when there is an error.\n\n### `props.onCatch` prop\n\n- Type: `(error: unknown, errorInfo: ErrorInfo) => void` in React; `(error: unknown) => void` in Vue; `(error: Error) => void` in Solid\n- Optional\n- A callback that will be called with the error that was thrown by the component's children.\n\n## CatchBoundary returns\n\n- Returns the component's children if there is no error.\n- Returns the `errorComponent` if there is an error.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { CatchBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <CatchBoundary\n      getResetKey={() => 'reset'}\n      onCatch={(error) => console.error(error)}\n    >\n      <div>My Component</div>\n    </CatchBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: catchBoundaryComponent\ntitle: CatchBoundary component\n---\n\nThe `CatchBoundary` component is a component that catches errors thrown by its children, renders an error component and optionally calls the `onCatch` callback. It also accepts a `getResetKey` function that can be used to declaratively reset the component's state when the key changes.\n\n## CatchBoundary props\n\nThe `CatchBoundary` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.getResetKey` prop\n\n- Type: `() => string`\n- Required\n- A function that returns a string that will be used to reset the component's state when the key changes.\n\n### `props.children` prop\n\n- Type: `React.ReactNode`\n- Required\n- The component's children to render when there is no error\n\n### `props.errorComponent` prop\n\n- Type: `React.ReactNode`\n- Optional - [`default: ErrorComponent`](./errorComponentComponent.md)\n- The component to render when there is an error.\n\n### `props.onCatch` prop\n\n- Type: `(error: unknown, errorInfo: ErrorInfo) => void` in React; `(error: unknown) => void` in Vue; `(error: Error) => void` in Solid\n- Optional\n- A callback that will be called with the error that was thrown by the component's children.\n\n## CatchBoundary returns\n\n- Returns the component's children if there is no error.\n- Returns the `errorComponent` if there is an error.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { CatchBoundary } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <CatchBoundary\n      getResetKey={() => 'reset'}\n      onCatch={(error) => console.error(error)}\n    >\n      <div>My Component</div>\n    </CatchBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
